## G. Known Limitations

- No historical backtest and no real-market performance evidence; parameters are unproven
  initial values.
- No live candle-closure guarantee: the module trusts the supplied `reference_time` and
  timestamps; it cannot verify the broker actually closed the candle.
- Strict freshness rule: a signal is only returned while
  `reference_time <= end of confirmation candle`, so a decision taken mid-next-bar is
  `stale_confirmation_candle`. Callers must evaluate at bar close.
- Strict timezone policy: naive timestamps are rejected, not assumed UTC.
- No Brain integration, no execution, no position sizing, no SL/TP, no risk attribution;
  no shared-state dedup store (caller must track `signal_id`).
- ADX warm-up requires `2·period` bars; the module uses a 50-bar floor for both timeframes.
- Tests ran on pandas 3.1.1 / numpy 2.5.4 / pytest 9.2.0 (Python 3.14), not the pinned
  `requirements.txt` versions, because the pinned wheels are unavailable for this
  interpreter. APIs used are standard and expected to work on pandas 2.2, but that
  combination was not executed here.

